     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of h3_0, h3_1 and h3_2, so all three must be cut. Cutting h3_0 (an AND step) needs one block, such as h1_0. Cutting h3_2 needs either blocking h3_2 itself or blocking both h1_2 and h2_2. h2_2 is always reachable from edge1, so no block on h3_0's side helps here. If h3_2 is blocked directly, h3_1 is still reachable through h1_2 and needs its own block. So 2 blocks can never be enough. A working set of 3 is h1_0, h1_2 and h2_2. Blocking h1_0 kills h3_0. With h1_0 and h1_2 gone, h2_1 is unreachable. Then h3_2 and h3_1 have no reachable parents.\"}"
    }
   ],
